.bridgie/specs/statement-review/tasks.json:6:      "title": "Move the built-in rule table into packaged YAML under src/cma/rules/ (v1 frozen, validated on load, with id and hash); CMA_RULESET chooses the table; test: P7 under v1 equals today's M1-M16 on every fixture and synthetic case",
.bridgie/specs/statement-review/requirements.md:183:IF CMA_RULESET is set to v1, THEN THE SYSTEM SHALL categorise with the built-in rule table as it was before this change, and SHALL record v1 as the ruleset in every evidence record.
.bridgie/specs/statement-review/requirements.md:218:For any committed synthetic case and test fixture, M1 to M16 under the new ruleset SHALL equal their values before this change, except on lines the change lists as newly recognised; under CMA_RULESET=v1 they SHALL equal them with no exceptions.
.bridgie/specs/statement-review/design.md:57:**Sub-decision: where the categorisation rules live.** (i) Keep them as code and add more. (ii) Move the rule tables into packaged, validated data files like the policy YAML; the matching passes (reversals, round trips, pairing, profile names) stay in code. *Chose (ii)*: the lists of acquirers, lenders, cash wording and gambling operators are what changes most often, the v1 table can be kept as data for rollback, and a firm's own rules use the same format.
.bridgie/specs/statement-review/design.md:168:- **Platform.** *Blast radius:* one Python package; new optional parts; the evidence JSON gains fields; PolicyResult and the checkpoint allow-list do not change. *Old and new side by side:* `cma run` is untouched, new commands are additive, and CMA_RULESET=v1 reproduces today's categories, cash included. *Resources:* files on disk only; no tables, queues, cron jobs or IAM. *Rollback:* an environment flag (CMA_RULESET), a config flip (show_policy_verdict) or a reinstall, with no data repair. *Observability:* see that section.
.bridgie/specs/statement-review/design.md:256:- Environment variables: CMA_HOME (case root) and CMA_RULESET (v1 or v2).
.bridgie/specs/statement-review/design.md:319:- Reversible: an older package ignores case folders it does not know and reads the v1 evidence keys it knows. CMA_RULESET=v1 brings back the old categorisation, with cash falling to OTHER, without a reinstall.
.bridgie/specs/statement-review/design.md:324:- CMA_RULESET: becomes v2 by default once evals and P7 pass; v1 restores today's categorisation exactly, including cash falling to OTHER.
.bridgie/specs/statement-review/design.md:331:2. Land the v2 tables (cash wording included), buckets, monthly summary and indicators behind CMA_RULESET. Make v2 the default when evals and truth for the new synthetic features pass, the cash truth included.
.bridgie/specs/statement-review/design.md:337:**Rollback.** For the policy check, set show_policy_verdict off. For categorisation, cash included, set CMA_RULESET=v1 or reinstall the previous wheel. Packs and evidence are immutable and record their ruleset, thresholds, policy hash, the show_policy_verdict setting and package version, so nothing needs repair. The old version leaves case folders written by the new one alone.
